# gate/ holds two different kinds of thing, and only one of them is tracked.
#
# TRACKED: the gate's own working material — the question it asks (prompts/) and
# the declaration of how it asks it (method.yaml). Those are reviewed.
#
# IGNORED: everything a RUN produces — the resolved baseline, the release delta,
# the rendered site text, the per-surface captures, the run manifest. Those are
# evidence for one release and are re-produced from scratch every time; a copy of
# one left in the tree is precisely the "found on disk" input the freshness check
# exists to refuse, and committing one would make it look authoritative.
#
# This is the pattern viewer-tests/.gitignore already uses for site-text.json,
# and it is written as "ignore everything, then name what is tracked" so that a
# per-run artifact added later is invisible by default. The landing script's
# stray check reads `git status --porcelain --untracked-files=all`, which does
# not list ignored files but does list unignored ones and exits 2 rather than
# widening a write set — so an artifact that is not ignored here refuses the next
# lane's landing, whoever it belongs to.
*
!.gitignore
!method.yaml
!prompts/
!prompts/*.md
# subject.json is TRACKED, and it is the one per-run-written file that is. It
# records what this release froze its question to — the digest of surfaces.yaml
# at the first fan-out — so that a later round cannot widen the manifest without
# saying so. A freeze a run could regenerate is not a freeze, and a freeze git
# cannot see is one no human reviews; both are why it sits on this side of the
# line while every other artifact a run produces sits on the other.
!subject.json
